SM(608,{"n":"Revelation 1.1-8","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Revelation 1.1-8.mp3","d":2815.2,"s":[[0.32,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in biblical studies, and it's an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.16,"I'm sure we're going to breeze right through the book of Revelation because it's so clear and uh understandable, and no one will have any questions at all."],[29.04,"You know, as you flip through it in the Orthodox Study Bible, you may notice there's like more notes than text on most of the pages."],[36.72,"So I have a feeling uh it will it will not move that quickly."],[40.24,"Even though the Book of Revelation is actually not that long of a book."],[44.32,"Um, if you just go by the text."],[47.6,"I mean, it's certainly longer than 2nd and 3rd John or St."],[51.12,"Jude's Epistle, but it's not it's not super long, like compared to the Gospels, for example."],[56.4,"Um but um by way of brief, brief, brief uh reintroduction."],[64.44,"Uh remember, this is gonna be the account of a visionary experience that Saint John has while he's in exile on the island of uh Patmos, uh where there was a salt mine."],[79.0,"Uh and so we're also gonna see that he was he was likely not the only Christian there, uh, because there's gonna be a worship space, or at least a place where they gather for prayer."],[94.33,"Um the Christians uh on the island."],[97.85,"That space where he received the vision is still preserved."],[101.77,"There's a monastery next to it now, an Orthodox monastery uh on Patmas."],[104.33,"You can go and see that place uh directly if you go there"],[111.33,"Umish. Oh, okay."],[117.01,"Uh and so um, yeah, that's probably enough."],[121.97,"And we'll get some more here as we pick up."],[125.15,"Um so unless there are any other uh comments or preliminary questions or a bad weather report that I need to know about, uh, we'll go ahead and pick up in uh the Revelation of St."],[139.23,"John uh chapter 1, verse 1."],[144.91,"The revelation of Jesus Christ, which God gave him to show his serv.ants things which must shortly take place"],[155.27,"And he sent and signified it by his angel to his servant John."],[162.31,"So the first point here is what is being revealed in this revelation."],[170.08,"What is it a revelation of?"],[172.08,"Jesus Christ. Of Christ."],[173.52,"So it is Christ revealing. things that are going to happen in the distant future"],[182.88,"He's not revealing the end times."],[185.12,"He's not revealing some war in the future."],[189.36,"It's a revelation of Christ Hsimelf."],[192.0,"Which God gave him to show his servants"],[197.93,"But what is he showing his servants in revealing himself?"],[201.45,"Things which must shortly take place."],[205.05,"Shortly does not mean 2,000 years later."],[209.21,"Think it would go without saying, but some of you may have heard someone talking about the book of Revelation recently."],[216.01,"So it doesn't go without saying, apparently."],[218.25,"But this is important."],[220.39,"Things that must shortly take place."],[223.03,"Minimally, minimally, this means what should also be kind of obvious that this text that St."],[232.55,"John is writing down."],[234.24,"He's recording this vision so that the written record of this vision can be sent to, as we're going to see tonight, these seven churches where he's had this leadership role."],[247.56,"Okay. Which means that what's written here is going to be relevant to those people living in the first century in those churches."],[258.12,"There is a message here for them."],[261.93,"From Christ. An angel or messenger to St."],[267.73,"John to pass on to them."],[271.49,"So nowhere are we going to see where it says, okay, that was the stuff for right now."],[278.53,"The rest of this stuff, don't worry about a couple millennia from now, that's when the rest of this stuff is going to happen."],[288.21,"We're not going to see a gap."],[289.81,"We're not going to see."],[291.09,"So everything in this book, the book of Revelation, is addressed to those people."],[300.85,"That doesn't mean, and it's addressed to them in the same sense that St."],[305.81,"Paul's epistles were addressed to the churches he sent them to."],[310.29,"Now that doesn't mean it's irrelevant to us."],[313.65,"It doesn't mean that we're reading it like as archaeology or something"],[316.63,"Like, oh, isn't this an interesting historical thing?"],[322.31,"So the book of Revelation, like the rest of the scriptures, is written for us, but it's not written to us."],[331.99,"Those are different things."],[334.71,"Because this is the revelation of Christ, and Christ is the same yesterday and today and forever."],[342.12,"Christ will also reveal himself to us through this book."],[351.0,"But it's not written to us as in we're the generation who finally can understand these things."],[358.78,"These things are all unfolding now in a way that they weren't before."],[365.1,"And this isn't just me picking on evangelicals."],[368.22,"I want to be clear about that too when I say this."],[370.98,"Because this isn't just contemporary evangelicals."],[374.18,"This has been all through church history."],[379.06,"Jonathan Edwards in the 18th century had this all worked out."],[384.59,"In terms of the geopolitics of his day, who was what?"],[388.11,"Martin Luther had this all worked out."],[390.75,"The Pope was the Antichrist, and he had the whole thing."],[394.05,"And the Prussians and this and that."],[397.17,"So this is this has happened over and over again."],[401.53,"As we're coming up on the year 1000 AD, people all over Europe sold their possessions and went on pilgrimages because they were totally sure, hey, thousand years, round number."],[414.87,"Christ was gonna return."],[416.23,"Now it's all happening."],[417.67,"Okay? They were wrong."],[419.27,"So I'm not picking on the contemporary people who do this any more than I'm picking on any other generation of Christians who have done this."],[428.53,"So as this goes on, though, I'm not only gonna argue that all of those folks were wrong, I'm also gonna argue that in a certain sense they were all right."],[441.78,"Because it's not just that, yes, obviously, Christ didn't return in the 18th century or the 16th century or the 11th century."],[452.75,"But it's also that the things that we're gonna see in the book of Re Revelvelationation. we talked last time about what apocalyptic is, what is"],[460.87,"The spiritual realities that are depicted here that St."],[464.39,"John sees and that he relates are spiritual realities all through history."],[473.03,"This is the story of spiritual reality in this last age before Christ's return, which all of us have been living in over the past 2,000 years."],[482.07,"So all of were in one sense right and in one sense wrong. the crazier ones"],[490.39,"Like Jack Van Impe saying Juan Carlos, King of Spain was the Antichrist."],[494.87,"He just kind of missed that one."],[496.23,"Because Juan Carlos didn't even do anything."],[498.31,"So, but for the most part, they've been identified"],[503.97,"The people who thought that Napoleon was the Antichrist were right in a certain sense."],[509.41,"He was one."],[511.41,"The people who thought Hitler was the Antichrist were right in a sense he was one."],[516.23,"Not the final one."],[517.85,"But right. So the spiritual realities that they're connecting with, they're they're right in a certain sense, but wrong about sort of the finality of it."],[528.99,"We're going to see that sort of all the way through here."],[531.23,"And so we're as we go through, we're we're I'm going to start with okay, here's what this is talking about in the first century."],[542.75,"We have to understand that first, and then we can move from there to how does that speak to us today?"],[550.15,"How do we relate to that today?"],[552.55,"You can't just we can't just leap."],[556.11,"And and that's true not just for Revelation, it's true for all the scriptures, but because people have pegged Revelation as prophecy and they have a certain understanding of prophecy, they tend to interpret it in a way that they don't interpret anything else, in a sort of ahistorical way that they don't interpret anything else."],[576.75,"So that's verse one."],[583.39,"Verse 2: who bore witness to the word of God."],[588.13,"So this is talking about Saint John now."],[591.53,"Who bore witness to the word of God."],[594.41,"Word there should be capitalized."],[597.13,"By the way, because this is Saint John we're talking about."],[601.69,"And to the testimony of Jesus Christ, to all things that he saw."],[608.73,"Now, this is all past tense."],[612.17,"At the beginning here, uh, people have a tendency to kind of ignore the verb tenses here and say, oh, well, it's just saying in this book, he's bearing witness to the things he saw in the vision."],[627.68,"But that's not actually how the verb tenses are structured here."],[630.72,"This is actually a reference to his gospel."],[635.0,"You won't find a lot of people talking about that because, like we talked about last time in the introduction, people want to say it's a different John."],[643.32,"They don't want to say it's the same author as the Gospel."],[648.92,"As I argued last time, and we'll see as we go through it's the same person."],[653.72,"Because we're going to see, even as we go through that the book of Revelation is structured the same way like his epistles were structured when we went through those fairly recently."],[663.88,"Oh, it's been a while on the gospel."],[665.24,"It's been five years on the gospel, but it's the epistles we went through relatively recently."],[672.12,"And so this is talking, this is identifying who this John is."],[676.44,"It's telling us that it's St."],[677.84,"John the Apostle."],[681.22,"Who bore witness to the Word of God."],[682.9,"How does his gospel start?"],[685.54,"In the beginning was the Word."],[687.07,"This is Logos."],[687.95,"It's the same word."],[689.6,"And then gave testimony of Jesus Christ."],[692.78,"To all the things that he saw."],[695.42,"So that's talking about the gospel."],[700.62,"Verse 3 Blessed is he who reads and those who hear the words of this prophecy, and keep those things which are written in it, for the time is near."],[710.14,"So notice the two pieces"],[717.82,"So there's he who reads and those who hear."],[720.06,"We have to remember this is part of the same act."],[724.68,"Because people weren't literate."],[727.18,"It wasn't that he was going to make, you know, a hundred thousand copies and get on the Ephesus Times bestsellers list."],[734.15,"By selling a tons of copies of this book, because everybody was going to sit at home and read it."],[738.07,"Most people couldn't read."],[738.95,"So this is going to be read publicly."],[741.45,"So this is the one who reads and those who hear."],[744.17,"So someone's going to come to their church, if they're in one of these seven cities, with this text and read it to them."],[750.09,"So blessed is the one who reads."],[752.25,"Blessed are those who hear."],[754.55,"But then notice part two and keep those things which are written in it."],[760.23,"And this keep is not like remember."],[762.71,"This week Intellectually."],[764.93,"Like, oh yeah, I forgot that part."],[768.27,"This is keep like keeping commandments."],[773.16,"So this is the same kind of hearing and doing idea that we got from Christ in the Gospels over and over again."],[784.7,"Say Paul and Romans, it's not the hearer of the law, but the doer that's justified."],[789.68,"We saw in St."],[790.56,"James's Epistle. So this also should condition how we look at this book."],[797.84,"That if we really hear this book or read it with understanding, it's going to require action from us."],[805.2,"So this isn't a book of intellectual curiosities"],[812.84,"This isn't a book of sort of fascinating predictions of the future."],[816.76,"This isn't like reading Nostradamus."],[819.14,"This is there is this is scripture."],[822.66,"It's like the prophecy in the Old Testament."],[827.46,"Even when we think about Old Testament prophecy, we tend to think of like, oh yeah, they predicted stuff that was going to happen in the future."],[833.78,"That's not really most of what the prophets did if you read the prophets of the Old Testament."],[839.7,"Unless you mean by that, the prophet showing up and saying, God's going to wipe you all out if you don't repent."],[844.74,"I mean, technically that is a prediction of the near future."],[848.16,"But the point is a moral one."],[849.12,"point is. The a moral one"],[853.12,"And if you actually heard what the prophet was saying, that would then require action from you, namely repentance in that kind of situation."],[861.22,"That you would you would change."],[863.3,"So again, we're we have to read Revelation the same way we read other scriptures."],[869.48,"That if we read this and we understand it, it's gonna require us to change how we live and what we do."],[875.08,"There's gonna be a response required from us."],[878.86,"If we want this blessing."],[882.46,"So it's not just saying you will be magically blessed if you read three chapters a day."],[887.76,"Like of this book."],[890.21,"Saying the blessing of God will come. if you really hear it, and then you put into practice what you've learned from Christ"],[903.77,"So we've talked about what does the time mean?"],[907.21,"Yeah. When we have the definite article."],[910.17,"We talked about the day."],[912.89,"I think we've also seen the time."],[915.95,"So one place where we see the time is uh the gospel reading that we hear all too often in the Orthodox Church."],[925.07,"Uh, because I have to come up with a different sounding sermon every time, uh, of Christ casting the demons into the pigs."],[932.53,"And I recycle my deviled ham joke every year."],[935.81,"And uh the uh when they see the demons see Christ coming, they say, Are you here to torment us before the time?"],[949.98,"So there is the day or the time, and that is a way in the scriptures that refers to the end."],[959.55,"The end. So the end is near has a slightly different ring to it."],[965.03,"Um, we also have to have to talk about what near means."],[971.49,"Because a lot of people will come to this and say, Oh, the time is near."],[974.77,"Say, John thought you know Christ was about to return."],[979.23,"Or, you know, whatever generation this is for is when Christ is about to return."],[985.63,"Um, but near, does not necessarily mean uh extension in space or time."],[996.05,"Let me give you an example."],[998.13,"If we say that Christ is near, do we mean like he's nearby?"],[1009.81,"Do we mean like he's about to show up?"],[1012.93,"No, but if I say Christ is near to each of us, you know what I mean."],[1018.82,"Even though if you try to parse that out in terms of time and space, it doesn't make a lot of sense."],[1024.31,"But you still know what I mean."],[1026.39,"And so this is as conveying a similar kind of idea."],[1033.11,"So the end, the final judgment, the time when things are put in order, that time is near to all of us."],[1043.27,"Because for any one of us, it could at any moment return, but in that any one of us could face our end."],[1058.37,"At any moment."],[1060.21,"And so the idea here is that's why it comes after the one who hears it and who keeps it"],[1066.79,"The idea is there's a sense of urgency about you taking the action."],[1073.91,"Hearing it, understanding it, taking action."],[1077.19,"Because hearing and then procrastination is very easy."],[1083.83,"Yes, I ought to do that."],[1086.31,"And one of these days I will."],[1088.01,"Like one of these days I'll get around to repenting."],[1090.49,"I'll start taking this stuff more seriously."],[1093.37,"I'll start praying more."],[1094.49,"I'll start going to church more."],[1095.85,"I got a lot on my plate right now, but you know, I'll get there."],[1101.9,"And so it's to communicate the end is not somewhere far off in relation to you where you can procrastinate."],[1107.98,"So don't It's near."],[1114.11,"That's the idea."],[1120.91,"So verse 4."],[1123.55,"John to the seven churches which are in Asia."],[1127.39,"Grace to you and peace from him who is and who was and who is to come."],[1132.75,"And from the seven spirits who are before his throne."],[1136.75,"We'll pause there."],[1137.63,"Now you may notice that sounds like the beginning of a letter."],[1140.77,"We've just read a whole bunch of epistles."],[1142.37,"We've just read a whole bunch of letters."],[1143.49,"So they all kind of start that way."],[1146.26,"So in fact, that's how, that's how uh, or similar at least to how St."],[1150.98,"Um, and that's because this is a letter"],[1151.74,"John started his epistles that we just finished reading."],[1157.42,"I mentioned last time that this first part, I'm gonna talk about tonight and maybe next time too, um consists of seven basically cover letters."],[1171.18,"So this first part that we're reading um is a uh general letter."],[1179.44,"The rest of chapter one."],[1181.44,"So this is a letter addressed to all seven of them, and then starting in chapter two, there's gonna be one letter that's specifically to each church."],[1192.85,"And so when the person showed up with the copy of the text of Revelation, it would have at the beginning the general letter to all the seven churches, and then the letter to that particular church, and then it would go into the rest of the text."],[1212.81,"Once we get past, you know, I was gonna say past the first century, but since this was written around 95 or 96, that's pretty quick."],[1221.69,"But in the early second century, then, it all gets compiled."],[1227.02,"So we've got the general letter, then we've got all seven of the letters to the individual churches, and then we have the text of the book, is what we have in our in our New Testament."],[1236.86,"But this is sort of the cover letter where Saint John is going to address the churches in general, explain what this book is, try to give it some context, give an introduction, a little more pithy than mine last time."],[1252.34,"And then he's going to kind of directly apply it to those individual churches and what's going on there."],[1260.36,"And how it should affect them."],[1261.56,"Because we're gonna see each of those churches is dealing with different things, shall we say."],[1266.36,"It is doing better or worse."],[1269.0,"Now there is a weird early modern way of reading the book of Revelation."],[1277.24,"There's lots of weird ways to read the book of Revelation, let's be honest."],[1280.68,"There's a weird early modern one where they they tried to turn the seven letters. into like seven ages of the church"],[1287.68,"And tried to like track them onto church history somehow."],[1292.96,"And I mean, hey, they didn't have journals at the time or dissertations, so I don't really know what the exercise was about, but somebody thought this a fruitful exercise."],[1303.44,"The biggest problem with that, of course, is that once again, these are letters to actual churches full of actual people."],[1310.96,"How would they have thought, oh no, this letter that he wrote to us is actually a prediction of how the church will be between the years 1200 and 1450?"],[1322.48,"Well, that doesn't make a lot of sense."],[1325.33,"Um so a weird code."],[1327.73,"So no, these are just cover letters written to actual people who St."],[1328.85,"He's lived and worked in these communities, he founded a couple of these communities"],[1330.49,"John knows. And so they have a relationship."],[1338.89,"And he wants them, each of the churches, as they need to receive it, to hear it, put it into practice, and get what they need to get out of it."],[1349.94,"So uh the other thing I will note, well, two more things I'll note here in the introduction."],[1355.38,"So he says, Grace to you and peace from him who is and who was and who is to come."],[1360.5,"So the way that and that's the way it's always translated in English."],[1364.18,"Okay. There's a problem with the way it's translated in English."],[1369.22,"Because when you hear that, it sounds like. is, was, and to come"],[1374.3,"Is to come sounds like present, past, future."],[1378.11,"And I've even heard people do sermons and write things based on that."],[1385.87,"And try to connect that to the name Yahweh in the Old Testament."],[1390.35,"I mean see who is."],[1391.87,"Here's the problem with it."],[1394.11,"That who is to come is literally who is coming."],[1399.95,"Who is and who was and is coming."],[1403.87,"Like from point A to point B."],[1407.84,"So. So yeah."],[1411.2,"So that's not the future of to be."],[1414.9,"It's not. who is and who was and who will be"],[1418.62,"It's who is who he who is, who was and is coming."],[1425.02,"And why is that important?"],[1430.62,"Because in addition to weeding out those bad over interpretations."],[1437.15,"He who is."],[1438.92,"Oh, and is a Greek translation of Yahweh."],[1444.54,"So that's where he starts."],[1446.22,"So he's clearly talking about not just any God."],[1449.18,"He's talking about the God of Israel."],[1451.36,"The Old Testament."],[1452.32,"God of the Old Testament."],[1454.21,"And that was, then, is a reference back to the Old Testament, the Old Covenant."],[1462.59,"And then who is coming?"],[1465.91,"Refers to uh God visiting."],[1470.63,"I know we've talked about this before."],[1472.31,"This is language you see a lot of times in the prophets."],[1475.03,"It says God will visit his people."],[1478.55,"Or he will visit their iniquities upon them."],[1481.69,"And we hear visit, we think, oh, isn't that nice?"],[1484.25,"He's coming for a visit."],[1485.39,"We'll set out a nice, you know, potluck."],[1488.36,"Uh this is less like that, and more like wait till your father gets home kind of visit."],[1495.54,"Like he's going to come visit and he's going to sort some stuff out."],[1499.27,"Things are gonna be quite literally."],[1501.53,"Justice is gonna happen when he shows up."],[1504.23,"So you need to prepare for his visit in the sense that you want to be on the right side of that visit, so it's a pleasant visit, and not on the wrong side of that visit, so it's an unpleasant visit where you get straightened out."],[1516.92,"Um, so that's how the day of the Lord is talked about."],[1521.34,"The day of the Lord, literally the day of Yahweh in the Hebrew."],[1523.74,"That's how it's talked about in the Old Testament."],[1527.54,"So he's talking about God, he's talking about God coming."],[1533.26,"And doing this."],[1534.5,"But by saying that, by applying that to God."],[1537.56,"He's talking about God the Father here, because he's about to talk about Christ."],[1541.84,"But he's connecting what we would call the second coming of Christ to the coming of God."],[1549.76,"He's uniting those two things as one event."],[1557.6,"So, and we'll see that here as we go forward."],[1560.64,"Also, the seven spirits who are before his throne."],[1567.36,"This is another thing where people like you notice they capitalized spirits."],[1577.84,"So I think it's because people are trying to make this Trinitarian."],[1584.18,"Yeah. well, that's the problem"],[1587.18,"So you've got God the Father and you've got Christ, in the next verse."],[1591.92,"And so they're like, hey, there's the word spirit."],[1599.04,"Let's try and make that the Holy Spirit."],[1601.36,"And then you get sort of lengthy sort of prognostications on how the Holy Spirit is sevenfold, or seven is the number of perfections."],[1613.12,"So it's saying the Holy Spirit is perfect, and then you're like, yeah, but it's still plural."],[1618.5,"Um, and the basic problem with that is that this has a very obvious referent"],[1625.78,"It's just people aren't that familiar with it."],[1628.18,"So if you want a place to look for this in the Orthodox Study Bible, you could go to the book of Tobit"],[1635.18,"When Saint Raphael shows up in the book of Tobit and identifies himself, he's sort of in disguise for a while."],[1642.54,"But when he identifies himself, he identifies himself as Raphael, one of the seven angels who stands before the throne of God."],[1654.38,"And you find this all through Second Temple Jewish literature."],[1660.14,"That there are seven archangels, arch meaning chief."],[1663.91,"There are seven chief angels who stand before the throne of God."],[1667.83,"Their names are listed all over the place."],[1669.99,"In Second Temple Jewish literature, the church fathers, all the way through to late antiquity, lists the seven archangels."],[1677.47,"We have the synaxis of the holy archangels."],[1680.35,"Um aren't as well known as St."],[1683.95,"Michael, St. Gabriel, St."],[1685.71,"Raphael. There's also St."],[1687.07,"Uriel. Then the other three names shift around."],[1690.75,"But so they're seven, they're described as standing before the throne of God."],[1698.19,"So when you see the seven spirits who are before his throne, before the throne of God, Jewish people reading this in the first century would have said, Oh, this seven archangels."],[1711.39,"That's not to deny the Trinity, it's just to say he's not talking about the Holy Trinity"],[1716.73,"Right here. Not the plural"],[1717.33,"There are going to be places where he talks about the Holy Spirit."],[1720.05,"He uses Spirit in the singular there."],[1723.62,"So that shouldn't be capitalized."],[1726.98,"But is he thinking maybe there's a spirit assigned to each church?"],[1730.9,"Well, there are seven angels for the seven churches that he's going to get to."],[1736.18,"But he doesn't identify them as the archangels in particular."],[1744.34,"So then, verse 5."],[1747.06,"And from Jesus Christ, the faithful witness, the firstborn from the dead, and the ruler over the kings of the earth."],[1756.02,"Even though it's not the end of the verse, we'll pause there because they actually did a good paragraph break there in the New King James."],[1763.9,"Okay, so now from Christ, and how is he identified?"],[1768.94,"The faithful witness."],[1772.67,"Why is why would St."],[1774.27,"John identify him as a witness?"],[1778.91,"You need two witnesses to establish the truth of something."],[1783.25,"So he's got God the Father, and he's got Christ."],[1787.17,"That's two witnesses to what he's about to tell them."],[1792.29,"He's also the firstborn from the dead."],[1795.57,"So he's seeding in here the eye of the idea of the resurrection already."],[1800.38,"That it's not just that Christ rose from the dead, and that's amazing and wonderful."],[1806.28,"But first fruits, the first fruits is the first of your crops."],[1810.06,"So when the first of your crops springs up, you're like, good."],[1814.4,"We're gonna have a harvest this year."],[1816.16,"They didn't all die."],[1817.82,"So that's the beginning of something bigger."],[1820.71,"And so Christ's resurrection is the beginning of the resurrection in the broad sense."],[1827.69,"Not just of all of humanity, but of the whole cosmos."],[1831.23,"Being restored and transfigured."],[1834.67,"And then, and the ruler over the kings of the earth."],[1838.61,"Who are the kings of the earth in this case?"],[1840.93,"Domitian. Sort of includes Domitian, yes."],[1848.89,"But what he's really got in view here are the demonic powers."],[1854.49,"Which includes Domitian because he was worshipped as a god."],[1858.46,"And the genius of the emperor, as it were, which the word genius originally meant sort of a spirit, a uh divine spirit that possessed certain individuals."],[1870.53,"So when you call someone a genius, you're calling them a demoniac, technically."],[1874.21,"Um but that line in Greek and Roman culture didn't exist, essentially."],[1881.19,"So Socrates says at a couple points in Plato's dialogues that he's possessed by a demon, and that creeps us all out."],[1888.63,"In fact, at one point it's really creepy"],[1889.44,"But they understood it differently."],[1893.2,"He says he has a demon that whispers wisdom to his soul."],[1897.52,"That kind of freaks you out."],[1898.98,"Um, but so but that was seen as a good thing."],[1902.75,"This is the touch of the divine."],[1904.61,"That's why they have this wisdom that seems supernatural."],[1907.17,"That's why they have this power in the case of the Roman Emperor that seems superhuman."],[1912.19,"Um, so yeah, they viewed that as a good thing."],[1915.47,"You see that a little bit in um uh the book of Acts, when there's the the enslaved woman who's demon possessed, whose owners are using her as a fortune teller to make money, and uh they cast the demon out of her, and then the owners are. mad because they're like, Man, we were making good money"],[1935.91,"But it was the same kind of thing."],[1937.45,"That kind of oracular power came from this."],[1943.61,"But so it's it's related to Domitian that he was seen to be sort of the human end of this divine rule, which, from the perspective of early Christians like St."],[1955.85,"John, was actually demonic rule."],[1957.87,"The imperial rule of Rome was not divine in a sense of being holy or godly or wonderful, but but demonic and oppressive."],[1967.48,"And so this is connected to Christ's ascension and enthronement."],[1973.78,"Before he ascends at the end of St."],[1975.14,"Matthew.'s gospel, he says, All authority in heaven and on earth has been given to me"],[1981.1,"So the idea here, this is another idea."],[1983.98,"We talked about how in epistles you lay the groundwork, you cede the ideas."],[1988.88,"So part of the idea here is that in Christ, God is taking back the world from those who claim to rule it."],[2000.45,"And it's now going to be returned to sort of his direct rule."],[2005.33,"And so that's already happened in the enthronement of Christ."],[2010.29,"We're gonna see how that plays out as the book continues."],[2014.13,"But St. John is seeding that here."],[2019.05,"And he continues to him who loved us and washed us from our sins in his own blood."],[2025.93,"So this is again Christ who loved us and washed us from our sins in his own blood."],[2032.73,"Note for the record how Christ's blood works vis-a-vis sin here again."],[2038.81,"It's not he who appeased the wrath of his father who hated us and wanted to destroy us."],[2045.35,"It's not that God was thirsty for our blood but took Jesus instead."],[2050.47,"It's that Christ's blood has washed us and purified us."],[2055.6,"And restored us."],[2057.22,"And we saw that same language, remember, in 1 John."],[2060.1,"One of many connections."],[2061.38,"This is how St."],[2062.02,"John. always talks about Christ's blood"],[2065.26,"He's analogizing the actual Day of Atonement, where the blood of the one goat was taken and used to purify the tabernacle."],[2078.38,"Verse 6, it has made us kings and priests to his God and Father."],[2082.86,"To him be glory and dominion forever and ever."],[2085.74,"Amen. We did Hebrews, so I won't go down a whole Melchizedek rabbit hole here."],[2099.68,"But the idea here is that uh not only is kingship and priesthood reunited in Christ. but that's passed on to all of us"],[2111.56,"Because remember, the promise back when the first covenant was given at Mount Sinai was that they would become a kingdom of priests."],[2121.16,"That didn't pan out so well."],[2123.93,"But then uh Saint Peter, as we saw, 1 Peter takes that and applies that to Christians, to Christians in the church."],[2134.03,"It says you're a royal priesthood."],[2136.27,"It's that same language of king and priest reunited, but they're reunited in Christ."],[2141.23,"They weren't reunited in ancient Israel."],[2143.39,"They didn't pull it off."],[2144.43,"In fact, they were split."],[2145.64,"The king and the priest, priesthood were completely separate."],[2149.02,"But they they're're reunited in Christ."],[2149.34,"'re John is saying that, and again, we setting the table for what's going to come."],[2151.22,"And so that means St."],[2158.42,"It's not just that Christ now has rule and dominion over the cosmos, but that's administered through his people."],[2168.34,"So what he's doing in reclaiming the world, reclaiming the creation for God, he's doing that through us as Christians."],[2182.34,"And how is he doing that through us?"],[2184.02,"Through us going around and conquering, for through us going and having a revolution against the Romans."],[2189.62,"That didn't go so well when they tried it three times."],[2193.92,"It went increasingly worse, in fact."],[2198.16,"No, it's through priesthood."],[2201.46,"It's through priesthood."],[2202.42,"It's through taking the world, taking the creation, taking the things of the world, and offering them back to God."],[2210.02,"Offering ourselves to God, offering our lives to God, offering each other to God."],[2216.6,"In doing that, we then redeem them."],[2220.85,"We bring those things back under God's rule."],[2230.05,"And notice he ties it back around."],[2231.71,"He started out with God the Father, went to Christ, and then ties it back around. to God the Father"],[2239.85,"So he doesn't have them separate off over here, but he's deliberately bringing them together."],[2246.81,"Not saying they're the same person."],[2249.82,"But they also aren't separate."],[2253.55,"In St. John's mind."],[2258.43,"Verse 7. Behold, he is coming with clouds, and every eye will see him, even they who pierced him, and all the tribes of the earth will mourn because of him, even so, Amen."],[2274.27,"So this is talking about Christ again, the he."],[2283.11,"So this is a particular reference."],[2289.27,"The cloud thing."],[2290.23,"And it's not just to the fact that when Christ ascended into heaven, remember, he ascended sort of on a cloud, and they said he'll come back the same way."],[2298.71,"This isn't just, oh yeah, he's going to come back out of the sky."],[2302.92,"God's up there in the sky somewhere."],[2304.6,"That's not what it's going for."],[2305.96,"This is a reference back to the book of Daniel, where the Son of Man comes riding a cloud before the ancient of days."],[2317.32,"And so when Christ refers to the coming judgment in the Gospels, he'll talk about when the Son of Man comes on the clouds of heaven."],[2325.48,"This is actually an image that's taken from Baal worship"],[2332.0,"Baal was the cloud rider."],[2334.08,"And so Daniel kind of steals that and says, that's not him."],[2342.08,"But uh so when it's talking about him coming on the clouds, this is talking about him coming in judgment."],[2349.92,"This is talking about him coming as the son of man with his angels to judge the world."],[2354.24,"And remember, judging means putting things back in order."],[2358.72,"Which is a good thing if you're oppressed, not great if you're an oppressor."],[2363.17,"Great thing if you're righteous, not a good thing if you're wicked."],[2366.47,"That everything gets put back."],[2367.91,"Last or first and first or last."],[2370.13,"As a result of this sort of sorting out."],[2373.97,"Okay. And notice also, every eye will see him."],[2379.65,"Now I'm picking on evangelicals."],[2383.49,"You can't have a secret rapture if every eye sees him."],[2388.99,"Can't have people just disappearing and leaving their clothes."],[2392.59,"Lawnmower running across the yard, planes crashing out of the sky because the pilot was a Christian."],[2401.31,"Every eye will see him when this happens."],[2405.47,"And notice, even they who pierced him."],[2409.07,"That is a reference to the crucifixion, but it's actually a very specific reference, not just to the book of Deuteronomy, but to the Greek version of the book of Deuteronomy."],[2422.87,"Uh at the end of in Deuteronomy twenty-eight through thirty, it lays out it's the end of Moses' sort of final sermon to the people of Israel before they go into the promised land."],[2435.75,"And it ends with him setting out blessings and curses."],[2438.55,"He says, Today I set before you blessings and curses, and you must choose."],[2442.47,"Everybody chose curses."],[2444.39,"You wouldn't think they would, but they all did."],[2448.27,"He says, This is what will happen if you keep the covenant."],[2451.48,"You obey the commandments."],[2453.16,"This is what'll happen if you don't."],[2455.48,"At the end of what'll happen if you don't."],[2458.02,"At the end of the litany of all the horrible things that will happen."],[2461.38,"It says in the Hebrew, something roughly like your life will dangle."],[2470.5,"Meaning like dangle by a thread."],[2472.74,"And you will not understand."],[2477.06,"That gets translated into Greek."],[2479.54,"As you can tell from the way I just translated, it's kind of ambiguous, weird Hebrew."],[2485.12,"The way that gets translated into Greek is, and you will look upon the one you have pierced."],[2494.64,"Which uh early Christians, at least starting with St."],[2497.76,"John here in Revelation, connected that to Christ."],[2503.32,"That part of what would happen to Israel and later Judah, Judea, because they had turned their back on God and not kept the covenant and not kept the commandments, part of that curse was that when Christ came to them, they didn't recognize him."],[2522.76,"The Messiah finally came to redeem them, they didn't recognize him."],[2529.24,"And they ended up being party to his death."],[2534.52,"And so St"],[2538.17,"John is dropping in this little allusion, to Deuteronomy."],[2542.31,"So he's saying when he says all the tribes of the earth next."],[2550.28,"There's one way to read that, especially if you were a Jewish person reading this text, where you'd say, all the tribes of the earth, oh yeah, the nations, the Gentiles."],[2558.44,"Yeah, they got it coming."],[2561.05,"Yeah. You know, he's gonna show up and smite them and make them our slaves."],[2565.67,"Um, but Saint John kind of precludes that by saying, including those who pierced him."],[2575.35,"All the tribes, including the Jewish tribes, will all see him and will all be subject to judgment."],[2584.27,"And that those who pierced him because of the Deuteronomy reference is unambiguous."],[2588.11,"Everyone all included"],[2589.0,"In terms of who he's he's talking about."],[2594.92,"And notice they will mourn because of him."],[2597.94,"So uh you could call Saint John a pessimist about how obedient to the commandments of God he thinks the world is, but uh I think he's just being a realist."],[2609.38,"That is now."],[2613.86,"Verse 8: I am the Alpha and the Omega, the beginning and the end, says the Lord, who is and who was and who is to come, the Almighty."],[2624.26,"Once again, that's who is coming."],[2628.15,"But now here's something interesting."],[2630.35,"Who's talking there?"],[2635.95,"Yeah. Just as the Lord."],[2640.35,"Who are we just talking about?"],[2644.67,"Christ. That's who the He has been."],[2648.15,"Those who pierced him, they didn't pierce God the Father."],[2652.03,"So if this is Christ speaking, he says that he's the Alpha and the Omega, the beginning and the end."],[2657.17,"Beginning and the end of the Greek alphabet."],[2660.74,"Says the Lord."],[2662.26,"Who is and who was and who is to come."],[2666.82,"That's what they call what St."],[2669.06,"John called the Father back in verse 4."],[2679.04,"And so we talked about how the coming of Christ and the coming of God to visit his people is united here as the same event."],[2689.76,"But if Christ is also he who is, Oon in Greek, means he's also Yahweh."],[2701.81,"So we've got two persons here, minimally."],[2706.22,"Two persons who are Yahweh."],[2709.34,"Who are labeled as Yahweh."],[2712.94,"The God of Israel."],[2715.28,"So it's not just the Father. it's also the Lord"],[2720.3,"And we saw this God Lord language."],[2722.72,"All through the New Testament."],[2725.04,"One God the Father, one Lord Jesus Christ."],[2730.45,"So there's the connection."],[2733.46,"And that title Almighty is also title of God in the Old Testament."],[2737.7,"It's Pantocrator in Greek, all powerful, almighty."],[2747.06,"So this is fairly clearly."],[2750.66,"You get a lot of people who do special pleading here."],[2753.46,"It's like, no no, no no, no no, no no, no no,"],[2755.54,"This is the Father talking now."],[2757.88,"It's a big problem with that."],[2760.4,"Because remember, this is the revelation of Jesus Christ."],[2765.2,"That Christ gave to John."],[2766.88,"So why would you have the Father talking in the first person if Christ is the one giving the vision?"],[2774.29,"So it's pretty clear that for St."],[2776.85,"John here, Yahweh, the God of Israel, is at least two persons."],[2783.27,"God the Father and Christ."],[2785.67,"So this isn't something that gets made up in the fourth century."],[2788.39,"I know we've been through this before, but it bears repeated."],[2792.79,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2800.07,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2805.47,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":20.16,"lv":2,"h":"Setting up: length and Patmos","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Breeze right through\" Revelation - \"so clear... no one will have any questions\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Orthodox Study Bible: <b>more notes than text</b> on most pages → won't move quickly</li><li class=\"d0\">Book not that long: longer than <b>2-3 John, Jude</b>, short next to the <b>Gospels</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Brief reintroduction: <b>visionary experience</b> of St. John in exile on <b>Patmos</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>salt mine</b> there</li><li class=\"d1\">likely <b>not the only Christian</b> there - will see a worship / prayer space</li><li class=\"d0\">Place of the vision still preserved; <b>Orthodox monastery</b> next to it</li></ul>"},{"t":139.23,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 1:1 - Revelation of Jesus Christ","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:1</b> - \"revelation of Jesus Christ, which God gave him to show his servants things which must shortly take place\"</li><li class=\"d0\">First point: <b>what</b> is revealed? → <b>Jesus Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Christ revealing</b>, not things in the distant future</li><li class=\"d1\">not the <b>end times</b>, not \"some war in the future\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"a revelation of <b>Christ Himself</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Showing his servants - what? In revealing himself: <b>things which must shortly take place</b></li></ul>"},{"t":205.05,"lv":3,"h":"\"Shortly\" and the seven churches","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Shortly</b> does not mean <b>2,000 years later</b>\" - \"would go without saying, but apparently doesn't\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Minimally: John records the vision so the written record can be <b>sent to the seven churches</b> where he had a leadership role</li><li class=\"d0\">→ relevant to <b>1st-century</b> people in those churches</li><li class=\"d1\">message <b>from Christ</b> via <b>angel / messenger</b> to John to pass on</li><li class=\"d0\">Nowhere \"that was for now; the rest a couple millennia from now\" - <b>no gap</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Everything</b> in Revelation addressed to <b>those people</b></li></ul>"},{"t":300.85,"lv":3,"h":"Written for us, not to us","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Addressed to them the way <b>Paul's epistles</b> were addressed to churches</li><li class=\"d0\">Doesn't mean irrelevant to us - <b>not archaeology</b>: \"isn't this an interesting historical thing?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Written <b>for</b> us, but not written <b>to</b> us\" - different things</li><li class=\"d0\">It's the revelation of <b>Christ</b>, same <b>yesterday, today, forever</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Christ will reveal himself to us through this book</li><li class=\"d0\">Not written to us \"as the generation who finally can understand\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"things all unfolding now in a way they weren't before\"</li></ul>"},{"t":365.1,"lv":3,"h":"Every generation has it worked out","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Not just picking on <b>evangelicals</b>\" - all through church history</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Jonathan Edwards</b>, 18th c. - geopolitics of his day all worked out</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Martin Luther</b> - <b>Pope = Antichrist</b>; \"the Prussians and this and that\"</li><li class=\"d1\">approaching <b>1000 AD</b>: Europe sold possessions, went on <b>pilgrimages</b> - \"thousand years, round number\" - Christ to return</li><li class=\"d0\">\"They were wrong\" - not picking on any one generation</li></ul>"},{"t":428.53,"lv":3,"h":"Wrong, and in a sense right","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Argues: all wrong - <b>and in a sense all right</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Obviously Christ didn't return in 18th, 16th, 11th c.</li><li class=\"d0\">But: <b>spiritual realities</b> depicted here are realities <b>all through history</b></li><li class=\"d1\">story of spiritual reality in this <b>last age</b> before Christ's return - the past <b>2,000 years</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Crazier ones: <b>Jack Van Impe</b> - <b>Juan Carlos, King of Spain</b> = Antichrist - \"just missed that one... didn't even do anything\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Napoleon</b> = Antichrist: right in a sense - <b>he was one</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Hitler</b>: \"not the final one. But right\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Right about spiritual realities; wrong about <b>finality</b></li></ul>"},{"t":531.23,"lv":3,"h":"First century first","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Method: start with <b>what it says in the first century</b> → then how it speaks to us today</li><li class=\"d0\">\"We can't just <b>leap</b>\" - true of all scripture</li><li class=\"d0\">But because people pegged Revelation as <b>prophecy</b> with a certain view of prophecy, they read it <b>ahistorically</b>, \"in a way they don't interpret anything else\"</li></ul>"},{"t":583.39,"lv":2,"h":"1:2 - Who bore witness","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:2</b> - \"who bore witness to the word of God, and to the testimony of Jesus Christ, to all things that he saw\"</li><li class=\"d0\">About <b>St. John</b>; \"Word\" should be <b>capitalized</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Past tense</b> - people ignore verb tenses: \"he's bearing witness to what he saw in the vision\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not how verbs are structured → reference to <b>his Gospel</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Few say so because they want <b>a different John</b>, not same author as the Gospel</li><li class=\"d1\">same person; book structured like his <b>epistles</b> (recent) - Gospel \"been five years\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Identifies <b>John the Apostle</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Gospel: \"In the beginning was the <b>Word</b>\" - same <b><i>Logos</i></b></li><li class=\"d1\">gave testimony of Jesus Christ, all he saw = the Gospel</li></ul>"},{"t":700.62,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 1:3 - Blessed is he who reads","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:3</b> - \"Blessed is he who reads and those who hear... and keep those things... for the time is near\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Two pieces: <b>reads</b> and <b>hear</b> - one act</li><li class=\"d1\">people <b>weren't literate</b>; no \"Ephesus Times bestseller list\"</li><li class=\"d1\">read <b>publicly</b> - someone comes to church with the text, reads to them</li><li class=\"d0\">Blessed the <b>reader</b>; blessed those who <b>hear</b></li></ul>"},{"t":754.55,"lv":3,"h":"\"Keep\" means do","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Part two: <b>keep</b> what is written</li><li class=\"d1\">not remember intellectually: \"oh yeah, I forgot that part\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>keep like keeping commandments</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same <b>hearing-and-doing</b> as Christ in the Gospels</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Romans</b>: not the hearer of the law but the <b>doer</b> justified</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>James</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Conditions how we read: truly hearing → <b>requires action</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not \"intellectual curiosities,\" not \"fascinating predictions\" - \"not like reading <b>Nostradamus</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">it's <b>scripture</b>, like OT prophecy</li><li class=\"d0\">OT prophets: mostly <b>not predicting the future</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"God's going to wipe you out if you don't repent\" - technically a near-future prediction, but the point is <b>moral</b></li><li class=\"d1\">hear it → <b>repentance</b>, change</li><li class=\"d0\">Revelation read the <b>same way</b>: requires change in how we live</li><li class=\"d0\">Blessing not \"if you read three chapters a day\" - comes if you <b>hear and put into practice</b></li></ul>"},{"t":903.77,"lv":3,"h":"\"The time is near\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>The time</b> (definite article) - cf. <b>the day</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Gospel of <b>demons and the pigs</b>: \"Are you here to <b>torment us before the time</b>?\" - \"recycle my deviled ham joke every year\"</li><li class=\"d1\">the day / the time = refers to <b>the end</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"The end is near\" has different ring</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Near</b> doesn't necessarily mean extension in <b>space or time</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"John thought Christ was about to return\" - wrong reading</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>Christ is near to each of us</b>\" - you know what I mean, though it doesn't parse in time/space</li><li class=\"d0\">The end / <b>final judgment</b> is near to all of us - Christ could return any moment; <b>any of us could face our end</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Hence follows hearing and keeping: <b>urgency</b></li><li class=\"d1\">hearing + <b>procrastination</b> easy: \"one of these days I'll get around to repenting... praying more... church more... a lot on my plate\"</li><li class=\"d0\">End not far off where you can procrastinate - \"<b>it's near</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1120.91,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 1:4 - A letter to the seven churches","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:4</b> - \"John to the seven churches in Asia. Grace to you and peace from him who is and who was and who is to come, and from the seven spirits before his throne\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Sounds like start of a <b>letter</b> - same as <b>John's epistles</b>: this is a letter</li></ul>"},{"t":1157.42,"lv":3,"h":"The cover-letter structure","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Opening part (tonight, maybe next time) = <b>cover letters</b></li><li class=\"d1\">rest of ch. 1 = <b>general letter to all seven</b></li><li class=\"d1\">from <b>ch. 2</b>: <b>one letter to each church</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Copy delivered: <b>general letter → letter to that church → rest of text</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Written <b>95-96</b>; <b>early 2nd c.</b> compiled: general letter + seven letters + text = our NT</li><li class=\"d0\">Cover letter: John addresses churches, <b>explains the book</b>, context, introduction - \"more pithy than mine last time\"</li><li class=\"d1\">then <b>applies it directly</b> to each church</li><li class=\"d1\">churches dealing with different things - <b>better or worse</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1269.0,"lv":3,"h":"\"Seven ages of the church\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Weird early modern reading: seven letters → <b>seven ages of the church</b>, tracked onto church history</li><li class=\"d1\">\"they didn't have journals or dissertations\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Biggest problem: <b>actual letters to actual churches</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"How would they think it predicts the church between <b>1200 and 1450</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Just cover letters to real people John <b>knows</b></li><li class=\"d1\">lived and worked there; <b>founded a couple</b> of these communities</li><li class=\"d1\">relationship; wants each to hear, <b>put into practice</b>, get what they need</li></ul>"},{"t":1349.94,"lv":2,"h":"\"Who is and who was and who is to come\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Two more notes in the introduction</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:4</b> \"Grace to you and peace from him who is and who was and who is to come\"</li><li class=\"d0\">English translation <b>problem</b>: sounds like <b>is / was / to come</b> = present, past, future</li><li class=\"d1\">sermons built on it; connected to the name <b>Yahweh</b></li><li class=\"d0\">But \"to come\" = literally \"<b>coming</b>\" - <b>who is, who was, and is coming</b> - \"from point A to point B\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not</b> \"who will be\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Why important: weeds out bad over-interpretations</li><li class=\"d1\">\"He who is\" = <b>Greek translation of Yahweh</b></li><li class=\"d1\">starts with <b>God of Israel, the Old Testament God</b> → back to the <b>Old Covenant</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1462.59,"lv":3,"h":"\"Coming\" = God's visit","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Who is coming</b> = God <b>visiting</b></li><li class=\"d1\">language of the <b>prophets</b>: God will <b>visit his people</b>, visit <b>iniquities</b> on them</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"a nice visit, set out a potluck\" → \"<b>wait till your father gets home</b>\" visit</li><li class=\"d1\">he'll \"sort some stuff out\" - <b>justice</b> when he shows up</li><li class=\"d0\">Be on the <b>right side</b> of the visit</li><li class=\"d0\">= <b>day of the Lord</b> (<b>day of Yahweh</b> in Hebrew)</li><li class=\"d0\">Speaking of <b>God the Father</b> here, about to speak of Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">connects <b>second coming of Christ</b> to the <b>coming of God</b> - <b>one event</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1560.64,"lv":2,"h":"The seven spirits","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Seven spirits before his throne</b> - capitalized \"Spirits\" in translation</li><li class=\"d1\">people try to make it <b>Trinitarian</b>: Father, Christ next verse, so \"Spirit\" = Holy Spirit</li><li class=\"d1\">→ \"sevenfold\" Spirit, seven = <b>perfection</b> - \"but still plural\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Obvious referent, just unfamiliar: <b>Tobit</b> (Orthodox Study Bible)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>St. Raphael</b> reveals himself: \"one of the <b>seven angels who stand before the throne of God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Seven <b>archangels</b> (arch = chief) throughout <b>Second Temple Jewish literature</b>, church fathers, late antiquity</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Synaxis of the holy archangels</b>: Michael, Gabriel, Raphael, <b>Uriel</b>; other three names shift</li><li class=\"d0\">1st-c. Jewish readers: \"<b>seven archangels</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not denying the <b>Trinity</b> - just not the Trinity here</li><li class=\"d1\">later places use <b>Spirit singular</b> (no capital)</li><li class=\"d1\">maybe a spirit per church? Seven angels for the seven churches coming - but not identified as archangels</li></ul>"},{"t":1744.34,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 1:5 - Faithful witness, firstborn, ruler","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:5</b> - \"from Jesus Christ, the faithful witness, the firstborn from the dead, and the ruler over the kings of the earth\" - good paragraph break in NKJV</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Faithful witness</b> - why? <b>Two witnesses</b> needed to establish truth</li><li class=\"d1\">God the Father + Christ = two witnesses to what he'll tell them</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Firstborn from the dead</b> - seeds <b>resurrection</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>first fruits</b> = first of the crops: \"good, we'll have a harvest\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ's resurrection = beginning of the resurrection <b>broadly</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not just humanity - the <b>whole cosmos</b> restored and transfigured</li></ul>"},{"t":1838.61,"lv":3,"h":"Ruler over the kings of the earth","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Kings of the earth: includes <b>Domitian</b> - but really in view: <b>demonic powers</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Domitian <b>worshipped as a god</b>; the <b>genius of the emperor</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><i>genius</i> originally = <b>divine spirit</b> possessing individuals → \"call someone a genius, you're calling them a <b>demoniac</b>, technically\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Greek/Roman culture lacked the line: <b>Socrates</b> in Plato says a <b>demon whispers wisdom</b> to his soul - creepy to us, but <b>a good thing</b>, \"touch of the divine\"</li><li class=\"d1\">wisdom seems supernatural; Emperor's power seems <b>superhuman</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Acts</b>: enslaved woman with demon, owners using her as <b>fortune teller</b> - same oracular power</li><li class=\"d0\">Early Christians like John: Roman imperial rule = <b>demonic and oppressive</b>, not holy</li><li class=\"d0\">Tied to <b>ascension and enthronement</b>: Matthew - \"<b>All authority in heaven and on earth</b> has been given to me\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Seeding the idea: God is <b>taking back the world</b> from those who claim to rule it → <b>direct rule</b>; already happened in the enthronement</li></ul>"},{"t":2019.05,"lv":2,"h":"1:5-6 - Washed, and made kings and priests","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"To him who loved us and <b>washed us from our sins in his own blood</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Note how Christ's blood works vis-a-vis sin</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not</b> appeasing the wrath of a Father who hated us</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not</b> \"God thirsty for our blood but took Jesus instead\"</li><li class=\"d1\">blood <b>washed, purified, restored</b> us - same language as <b>1 John</b>; \"how John always talks about Christ's blood\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Analogy to <b>Day of Atonement</b>: blood of the one goat <b>purified the tabernacle</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2078.38,"lv":3,"h":"Kings and priests","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:6</b> - \"has made us <b>kings and priests</b> to his God and Father. To him be glory and dominion forever. Amen.\"</li><li class=\"d0\">(Did <b>Hebrews</b> - no Melchizedek rabbit hole)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Kingship and priesthood reunited in Christ</b> - and <b>passed on to all of us</b></li><li class=\"d1\">promise at <b>Sinai</b>: a <b>kingdom of priests</b> - \"didn't pan out so well\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>1 Peter</b>: \"<b>royal priesthood</b>\" applied to the church</li><li class=\"d1\">in ancient Israel king and priest were <b>split</b>, \"didn't pull it off\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ's rule over the cosmos <b>administered through his people</b> - reclaiming creation through us</li><li class=\"d1\">how? Not conquering or <b>revolt against the Romans</b> - \"tried three times, increasingly worse\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>through priesthood</b>: taking the world and its things and <b>offering them back to God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">offering ourselves, our lives, <b>each other</b></li><li class=\"d1\">→ we <b>redeem</b> them, bring them under God's rule</li><li class=\"d0\">Ties back to <b>God the Father</b> - not separate, \"not saying same person, but also aren't separate\" in John's mind</li></ul>"},{"t":2258.43,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 1:7 - He is coming with clouds","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:7</b> - \"Behold, he is coming with clouds, and every eye will see him, even they who pierced him, and all the tribes of the earth will mourn because of him. Even so, Amen\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Clouds</b>: not just the ascension (\"come back the same way\"), not \"God up in the sky\"</li><li class=\"d1\">reference to <b>Daniel</b>: <b>Son of Man</b> rides a cloud before the <b>Ancient of Days</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Christ in Gospels: Son of Man <b>coming on the clouds of heaven</b></li><li class=\"d1\">image taken from <b>Baal worship</b> - Baal the <b>cloud rider</b>; Daniel \"steals that\" - \"that's not him\"</li><li class=\"d0\">= coming <b>in judgment</b>, as Son of Man with his angels</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>judging = putting things back in order</b>: good if oppressed, not if oppressor; <b>last first, first last</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2373.97,"lv":3,"h":"Every eye will see him","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Every eye will see him</b>\" - \"now I'm picking on evangelicals\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>no secret rapture</b>: no disappearing and leaving clothes, lawnmower running, planes crashing because the pilot was a Christian</li><li class=\"d0\">Every eye sees when it happens</li></ul>"},{"t":2405.47,"lv":3,"h":"\"Even they who pierced him\" - Deuteronomy","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Pierced</b> = crucifixion; specifically <b>Greek Deuteronomy</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Deut 28-30</b>: end of Moses' last sermon before the promised land - <b>blessings and curses</b>, \"you must choose\"; \"everybody chose curses\"</li><li class=\"d1\">end of curses, Hebrew roughly: \"your life will <b>dangle</b> (by a thread) and you will not understand\" - ambiguous, weird Hebrew</li><li class=\"d1\">Greek: \"<b>you will look upon the one you have pierced</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Early Christians, from John here, connect it to <b>Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">part of the curse on Israel/Judah for not keeping covenant: when Christ came, <b>didn't recognize him</b>; <b>party to his death</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2538.17,"lv":3,"h":"\"All the tribes of the earth\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Jewish reader: tribes of the earth = <b>nations, Gentiles</b> - \"they got it coming... smite them, make them our slaves\"</li><li class=\"d0\">John precludes that: \"<b>including those who pierced him</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">all tribes, including <b>Jewish tribes</b>, see him, <b>subject to judgment</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Deuteronomy reference makes it <b>unambiguous</b> - everyone included</li><li class=\"d0\">\"They will <b>mourn</b> because of him\"</li><li class=\"d1\">John a pessimist about world's obedience? \"I think he's just being a <b>realist</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2613.86,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 1:8 - Alpha and Omega","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:8</b> - \"I am the <b>Alpha and the Omega</b>, the beginning and the end, says the Lord, who is and who was and who is to come, the <b>Almighty</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Again \"who is <b>coming</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Who's speaking?</b> The Lord - <b>Christ</b> (the \"he\" so far); those who pierced him didn't pierce the Father</li><li class=\"d1\">Alpha and Omega = beginning and end of the <b>Greek alphabet</b></li><li class=\"d1\">same title John gave the <b>Father</b> in v. 4</li><li class=\"d0\">Coming of Christ and coming of God to visit = <b>same event</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Christ is also \"<b>he who is</b>\" (<i>ho on</i>) → also <b>Yahweh</b></li><li class=\"d1\">→ <b>at least two persons</b> labeled Yahweh, God of Israel</li><li class=\"d0\">God / Lord language through NT: <b>one God the Father, one Lord Jesus Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Almighty</b> = OT title of God; <i>Pantocrator</i></li></ul>"},{"t":2747.06,"lv":3,"h":"Not the Father speaking","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Many do <b>special pleading</b>: \"no, this is the <b>Father</b> talking now\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Problem: this is the <b>revelation of Jesus Christ</b>, which Christ gave to John</li><li class=\"d1\">why would the Father speak in first person if Christ gives the vision?</li><li class=\"d0\">Clear: for John, <b>Yahweh, the God of Israel, is at least two persons</b> - Father and Christ</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Not something made up in the <b>fourth century</b>\" - \"been through this before, but it bears repeating\"</li></ul>"}]});
